I do believe that just detected a  comment section going straight to hell  so first off I want to say the response  to the video I made with my thoughts on  Jodie Whittaker being cast as the doctor  has been kind of unprecedented it's been  phenomenal honestly in terms of both the  the viewership the general reaction and  the comment section well mostly by and  large the comment sections have been  actually really interesting for me to  watch when they remained respectful  unfortunately they don't always but this  isn't really a comment response video  I'm not quite so self indulgent has to  get into those quite yet but um I do  want to address something that I kept  seeing get brought up in the comments  because I feel like it's something that  is not only not a great comparison but  making the comparison especially the way  people do as like it closes the book on  argument it is kind of distracting  something that I saw repeatedly brought  up by people who take at some degree of  issue with Jodie Whittaker playing the  doctor specifically in terms of the  doctrinal longer being portrayed by a  man is comparing it to the 2016 a reboot  of ghostbusters and I kind of want to  address that because like I said I don't  I'm not sure they've completely thought  this through and I just there's  something I just feel they need to point  out in the hope of calming some people  down a little bit now I again do have  concerns about Jodie Whittaker as the  doctor  I'm also very hopeful I'm certainly not  abandoning the show or anything like  that I might come back to that point as  well but I do have points of concern I  have expressed them in two videos now so  I'm not going to rehash all that but the  comparison to Ghostbusters 2016 doesn't  work for one mr. reason that was a  reboot now here's something about a  reboot  a reboot in a way kind of erases the old  film now not in any true practical way  as people who are often in favor of  these kinds of changes love to point out  no one's coming and taking away your old  versions of ghostbusters you just watch  that and let us do this well that's true  but at the same time what a reboot does  say is in this continuity nothing that  you loved about the original films  happened it doesn't count anymore if we  get to make any sequels to this we're  not going to acknowledge this and if we  have our way and this is successful  Ghostbusters will now mean this and it  will no longer mean the thing that it  used to be that you used to love now  that's not unique to ghostbusters that's  actually inherent in most reboots so the  reason it stuck out with ghostbusters so  much is that functionally story-wise  pretty much on every level there was no  need for it to be a reboot they would  have taken minimal tinkering with the  story to just have it be a continuation  not completely wipe out the old  continuity and then not piss off a whole  chunk of fans who often got loved would  be unfortunately incredibly loud and  very rude people just going no girls  allowed but their concern was really  over a feeling of legitimate loss  because they were being told that what  they loved doesn't count anymore  and again that's kind of what happens  with a reboot and it stuck out with  ghostbusters because that was and it  would visor reboot the the project may  have had you know it had other issues  going on as well  but I know that there was a whole  contingent of fans who took issue with  that movie not because it was women but  because there was no need for it to  completely erase the film that they  loved I was in that same camp now  ultimately when the film came out I  didn't hate as much as I thought I would  but it also wasn't great it was fine it  just kind of was but I don't want to  dwell too much on that but I just want  to make the point like what regeneration  is or actually more specifically what  regeneration is not is a reboot  regeneration is a wonderful thing that  is truly unique to Doctor Who  now I absolutely understand people who  have concerns about the doctor being  played by a woman as I said I have some  of my own I get people feeling some  degree of loss at the fact that the  doctor will no longer be portrayed by a  man I understand that people who are  making the decision that they will no  longer watch the show because the doctor  is going to be portrayed by a woman I  don't agree with that one but I  understand the root of the sentiment  even if I very surely don't agree with  it and I personally will be watching the  show but what I don't get is people  acting as if Jodie Whittaker playing the  doctor somehow erases the previous  incarnations of the doctor in fact I've  seen some comments where people  basically say that's what it does but it  isn't and again that's part of the  glorious thing about Doctor Who because  of how her generation works not only  does Jodie Whittaker playing the doctor  not erase any previous male version of  the doctor it actually can't exist  without them and I don't just mean in  the sense of all if there wasn't a  original we couldn't be still lesser I  mean gee just narrative Lee she could  not exist without all these previous  incarnations and Doctor Who as a show  has always been very quick to integrate  the past experiences of the doctor so  none of that's going away and more to  the point with something like  ghostbusters if they wanted to make it  male again they were going to have to  rearrange the new thing they just did if  for whatever reason this either doesn't  work or even if it does once she's  decided she's done with the part we can  get a man again we may or may not but  you can get it back so any sense of loss  that you get and one is you're willing  to not abandon the show all together is  going to be temporary now that's not me  minimizing your sense of loss if you are  feeling a sense of loss as the doctor no  longer being male but it's temporary  unless the show gets cancelled which is  the other thing that I'm seeing in the  comments that I really really don't  understand  I understand people who say that they  believe that this move will cause the  show to get canceled I don't agree but  fine I get that that's what you believe  will happen what I don't get is when I  see people who claim to be fans actively  wishing that the show will now fail and  get canceled because of this change I  would say I don't get that but I suppose  I do in the sense of they feel it will  validate their anger at this move but  I'm not sure of the people making that  particular leap like going beyond just  saying I won't watch this but actually  saying I hope the show gets cancelled  which again I know it's happening I'm  seeing it happen in my own comment  section I don't know if they've thought  that thought all the way through because  they're actually actively rooting for  something that they claim to love to die  and I know that I'm the guy who put out  a very ranty video screaming about how I  wanted Warner Brothers DCE you movies to  fail but here's the thing if you stuck  through that video all the way through  and let me get to my final point the  reason I wanted them to fail was so that  they would have to try again and the  reason they would be able to try again  is because the source material the comic  books weren't going anywhere whether the  movies were successful or not there  might be ancillary stuff for Doctor Who  there might be comic books there are  audios or other things but it's a show  first so when you root for the show to  die you're rooting for the source  material to go away you're rooting for  the foundation to end and I don't  understand that I never will and as I  said I do have my concerns with the  doctor no longer being a man but I root  for the show I will always room for this  show this is my favorite show on  television and I will always always tune  in because I want it to be great and  every episode that ever gets made I want  to watch so that I get  to see whether or not it's great and  when it's not great yeah it sucks and if  it ever becomes consistently not great  which I know some people feel under  Martha it did that sucks every new  episode is a chance for it to be great  and that's why I'm always going to come  back now again if you're making the  decision to bail on the show now I  personally don't quite get at least not  giving it a shot to see if it's working  for you but at the very least I would  think that even if you decide to not  watch for as long as Jodie Whittaker is  the doctor that you would still sit back  and go boy I hope it keeps going so that  it can become something that I love  again as opposed to sitting back and  going man I hope that thing that I used  to love dies because it'll validate my  feelings about this particular thing  that I don't think they should have done  so I think that's about it I don't know  if I just said something that was  insightful and helpful or that was  self-indulgent and incendiary and I  suppose the reaction that I get this one  will be my answer so your thoughts on I  guess what I just said  will have yours are your thoughts  continuing to change evolve on the  doctor becoming a woman are now that  we've had you know more time more days  to deal with it is your opinion  softening are you standing your ground  are you more excited are you less  excited whatever your thoughts are and  please keep them respectful I love  seeing discussions between people  disagree as long as no one is you know  shouting obscenities at each other so if  you can keep it civil drop something  down on the comments let's talk about it  don't forget to Like subscribe check me  out on Twitter I council of geeks give a  listen to the council of geeks podcast I  am also one half of the punch like a  girl podcast both of those are available  on iTunes and stitcher and until next  time this council is adjourned  [Applause]  [Applause]
 

